      "side": 1,
      "message": "@cmllamas@google.com\nThe reason why we use trace_android_vh_sync_txn_recvd() instead of trace_android_vh_binder_set_priority() is:\n1) trace_android_vh_binder_set_priority(t, task) cannot distinguish between being called by binder_proc_transaction() or binder_thread_read().\n2) We don\u0027t customize the priority adjustment in binder_proc_transaction() -\u003e trace_android_vh_binder_set_priority(t, task), but implement it in binder_proc_transaction() -\u003e trace_android_vh_binder_proc_transaction_finish(), which can consider the situations where there is thread, no thread, and pending_async.\n3) When a thread is selected in trace_android_vh_binder_proc_transaction_finish(), the priority of the binder_thread is raised before the thread is awakened.\n4) For sync binders, when no thread is selected in binder_proc_transaction() -\u003e trace_android_vh_binder_proc_transaction_finish() , the priority is raised again in trace_android_vh_sync_txn_recvd().",
